Yahoo!
Finally!!!
After 7 months I have finally ascended!!!!!!!
And I did it with a Healer.
Spoilers follow:

Did that ^L come out?

I was determined to do this the hard way, and after having cracked tourists
(a few embarassing incidents with drawbridges and cockatrice put paid to
my quest-completing tourists) I thought I'd have a go with a Healer.

This character looked a disaster area at first - best stat was CHA at 16,
but strength and INT were both 8! Very disheartening for a spell-casting
afficiando like myself, but only to be expected in a healer. An armour
store on level one outfitted me with boots of speed, which cheered me
up no end.

I staggered through the early levels in the way healers have to - running
away frequently and using potions and spells of healing without mercy. I
varied from my usual tactic of totally ingratiating myself with my God -
I've become Envoy of Balance rather too many times... This was also somewhat
forced on me by the fact that there was an altar on level one, and that was
the only randomly generated altar in the game. Fortunately, minetown had
an altar to Hermes, and before leaving I'd acquired MagicBane (Good call, 
Hermes!), which remained my primary (indeed only, except for Staff of
Ascelpius, which I never wielded - I've no idea what it's like as a 
weapon - it struck me as a bit incongruous) weapon for the rest of the
game. No hardware shop, sadly, but the lighting store had 7 candles going
at bargain-basement prices. (Good old charisma 16).

I reached level 23, which turned out to be the Medusa level, without 
undue haste, finding the portal to ludios on the way - but I quickly
retreated from there. At 23, I was almost killed on being ambushed by the titan
and retreated up a level to lick my wounds. I encountered a wraith, and
next moment was level 14, headed for the quest.

Took one look at the quest and squealed, having no means to travel over water.
Also, I had a pack full of unidentified items (no scrolls or potions yet id'd!)
I deduced id with a help of a local shopkeeper and headed back to level 1 to
that altar to check out blessed/cursed status and manufacture some holy water.
Eat a nymph on the way and was 'porting all over the place, but my newly
id'd pack contained a ring of teleport control. Sadly no levitation gear,
but I went back to that armour store & found some cursed boots I'd rejected.
One scroll of remove curse later and I had a pair of lev boots (-1). Not ideal
as I had to swap with my speed boots when I wanted to float, but still.

Completed the quest by 'porting very fast across all the levels I could do so.
Still had to pray twice to Hermes for healing!

Into Ludios with no ring of conflict, so killed the soldiers 1 by 1 (at end
of game: 122 soldiers killed! I thought someone said there were only 121 of
each type of monster). Also genocided ; as I'm paranoid about drowning. Croesus
very nearly did for me - I needed to #invoke the staff and pray to Hermes. Lots
of trouble with trolls regenerating faster than I could eat them. 

Used scroll of taming to get me a dragon (or two, but one died). Used pets
to clear out goldroom. Back to
minetown (pant, puff), pay priest for 9 point of protection, and get draggy
to sic him. No useful spellbooks, sadly.

Paid Oracle lots of money and got told how to use bell,candle,and book.(But
in a way that confused me). Whizzed back down & dodged medusa by a trapdoor,
then chased a master lich from the castle 3 levels below back up to there
and fought them both at once. Picked up lots of spellbooks now I was nearly
intelligent from sevel blessed gain abil  & enlightment potions. Cleared out
castle. Used WoW to  do something about my armour (still wearing elven chain)
and get me SoR. Had not yet found any enchant armour scrolls! Only decent
thing was CoD found (cursed) in minetown.
 Cleared vsalley of dead and found ring of levitation so I could ditch
the boots and stay fast (very fast as i'd zapped me with a wand of speed).
Found enchant armour scrolls. Wrote a few more and AC -27 for rest of 
game.
Priest of Moloch had spellbook of identify! yahay!. Realize two things:
1. Dip in ludios moat had wiped half my spell books - inc magic mapping.
Aargh. Had clairvoyance, but no idea what it did. As it turned out, acted
as reasonable substitute for mm till I found a new magic marker. 
2. No disintigration resistance! Aaargh. Where black dragon? Answer: Quest.
Another long trek. Draggy disintigrated almost immediately by black dragon.
Ulp! I'd never realized what a good thing it had been I hadn't stoped to
look around the quest levels. My AC was only -5 at the time - I would have
been caught easily.

So, finally ready to enter Gehennon! Dumped all not-immediately-useful
stuff to get me unenumbered, and in I went....My FIRST ENTRY TO GEHENNON!
Genocided cockatrices at this point cos I hate 'em.

Accidentally killed a peaceful Asmodeus (well, he was invisible) with a handy
wand of death they'd been shooting me with in the castle.
Lost a level in Orcus' home when the vampires surrounded me...
Juiblex no problem thanks to blessed unicorn horn (my constant companion).
Found a new magic marker on level 51, armed with which was able to map 
everywhere (blessed spellbook of mm). Vlad a push-over. Recruited large numbers
of monsters, thanks to blessed scroll of taiming, but all met various messy
ends defending their master. Wished many times I had another blessed genocied
scroll to off L's. Reached exp level 25. 
Killed wiz with wand of death (recharged). And again. Then things got tricky.
MEssed up candle, book, stuff, but got it sussed in the end. High priest
obligingly killed by moloch - idiot stood in way of m's lightening, which
was (AC -27) not very dangerous for me!
Fortuituosly found ring of conflict to even to odds.
Ran out as fast as I could, given the difficulties. Almost exhausted food 
supply, and failed to replenish at the castle.  Failed agin when abushed at the
food shop on level 3. Ran for stairs up & out!

Plane of Earth a great shock. Messed up good and proper trying various tactics
out. Had rings of poly & poly control, so uncursed poly ring & almost got self
killed as a xorn. Then forgot to put armour back on!!! Survived this, but after
much failed running around with digging wand (using telepathy to judge where
to go), tried again as elemental. Ambushing by vampire lord cost 5 experience
levels!!! (1 regained via potion, 2 by lucky polymorh later).
 Also killed me, but had at
least had forsight to wear AoLS. Two spare in my pack, as well. 

Archon would have put paid to me on Plane of Air, but I ran away. Rings of
conflict are my favourite item, I think. Found portal after running around a 
bit. Fire I lit up with handy blessed scrolls of light, and wandered into
the portal with no trouble. Water just messed around till ported out.

Astral plane nearly finished me from lack of food! Was constantly munching 
corpses despite being adjacent to evil things just to stay alive! Never
seen so many artifacts in my life before...
Second temple was Hermes'. Final victory!

2241 creatures killed, 4 species genocided. 3680080 points in 66341 moves.
Final stats: STR:18/30 (25 with GoP) DEX:17 CON:18 INT:14 WIS:18 CHR:17
I'd had them all 18 (except INT at 15) before my polymorphing got out
of hand.

I'm happy.

  Julyan.


